Z||000000||Shiner||11-09-1999||02:51 AM||||Guys, <BR>As you probably know, the Haynes manual STINKS!  I heard the Chilton was even worse.<BR>Where can I get a factory service manual for my '87 GT?  There is so much I would like to know, and the Haynes manual just doesn't cut it.  I mean, Haynes isn't bad if this is your first oil change EVER, or you need to know how to change the air filter.... but for wiring diagrams it just plain SUCKS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Greg Piet||11-09-1999||04:58 AM||||I got mine on Ebay for about 1/2 of what the fiero store sells them for.<BR>Mine however has a few grease stains on teh cover, and a black streak on the outside border from quickly going through pages.<P>The Fiero store sells them for 75 bucks a pop||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||11-09-1999||05:00 AM||||Try this website: <A HREF="http://www.lloydsautolit.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lloydsautolit.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||11-09-1999||08:33 AM||||You can get a CD set from  <A HREF="http://www.alldata.com" TARGET=_blank>www.alldata.com</A>  that is primarily based on the service manual for only $25.<BR>I have one and its pretty good, but the factory service manual would be the complete source.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-09-1999||12:04 PM||||I just got a response from Lloyds Lit.  They have one 1988 Factory Service manual left, and I was told it was their second inquiry on it today.  It has 900 pages, slightly used, and they want $89.  Not a bad price for one in good condition.||||reg||7
Z||000005||ggarsk||11-09-1999||05:44 PM||||Just keep checking e-bay. I goy a '84 Service Manual for $30. I always see some up for auction.<p>[This message has been edited by ggarsk (edited 11-09-1999).]||||reg||1
