Z||000008||Scott2M4||12-14-1999||12:47 PM||||My significant other just bought me that Popular Mechanics CD.  Unfortunately, I've been unable to get the software to dial up the PM site in order to download the info on my car.<P>Anyway, anyone have comments on the quality of this software?  How does it compare to the Haynes and Chilton books?  And, for those of you about to ask ... no, I don't have a computer in my driveway!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000009||mutfish||12-14-1999||03:03 PM||||I have both the ALLDATA software and the factory sevice manual...in my opinion buy the book,it's much more comprehensive.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||12-14-1999||05:24 PM||||I agree. I'm not terribly impressed with the ALLDATA disk. <BR>Something else to think about... I had my Mindspring account for nearly two years, and never got the *first* piece of SPAM mail, --until I registered that damned CD (requires an e-mail address). Of course, it could be a coincidence. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-14-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||12-14-1999||05:48 PM||||I noticed I never started receiving any spam until I registered here, now I get 5-10 a day.  But, it could also be coincidence. Or, maybe cliff <B> IS </B> making money off us <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.||||reg||7
Z||000012||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||10:24 PM||||What is the correct name of the "right" book to have?  I have the Chiltons, Haynes, and the CD, but I need more (insert small Tim Taylor grunt here).||||reg||1
Z||000013||Bill Osmer||12-15-1999||08:27 AM||||MonkeyMan, et al -<BR>IMHO, I've not been happy with any ONE of the common manuals Haynes, Chiltons or Factory Service. However, when you collect all three, the combination has covered all my needs so far. The Factory Service has the better electrical diagrams, but some of the better techniques are in the others. The best info the I get is right here, but it's difficult to drag my computer screen to the garage or under my Fiero when I need to work on it. So, the bottom line.... all 3 is what you should get.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||08:33 AM||||Speaking of electrical info I once had a VW manual that had all the wiring diagrams in color.  The Electrical items they conected to were actual drawings. best I,ve ever used.<BR>Coy<BR>||||reg||1
